  "answer_markdown": "For the POST `/v1/audio/speech` endpoint, the **required fields** in the `SpeechRequest` body are:\n\n- `model`: Specifies the model to use (e.g., `voxtral-mini-tts-2603`) [1].\n- `input`: Contains the **text to be converted into speech** [1].\n\nAdditionally, one of the following must be provided:\n- `voice_id`: A saved voice identifier for generating speech [1].\n- `ref_audio`: A base64-encoded audio clip for cloning a voice on the fly [1].\n\nThe `input` field specifically contains the **text prompt** that will be synthesized into speech [1]. This text should follow guidelines such as:\n- Being in the same language as the voice prompt for best results [2].\n- Avoiding rich formatting (e.g., markdown, emojis) [2].\n- Keeping prompts under 300 words [2].\n\nExample `SpeechRequest` body:\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"voxtral-mini-tts-2603\",\n  \"input\": \"Hello! This is Voxtral, Mistral's text-to-speech model.\",\n  \"voice_id\": \"your-voice-id\",\n  \"response_format\": \"mp3\"\n}\n```\n\n",
