{
  "answer_markdown": "To achieve both **automatic Organization joining** and **sign-in without separate password credentials**, the following mechanisms and plans are required, along with their prerequisites regarding a verified domain:\n\n### 1. **Automatic Organization Joining (Email Domain Authentication)**\n- **Supported Plans**: Team and above [1].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** is mandatory before enabling this feature [1][5].\n  - Users with email addresses matching the verified domain can join automatically via [Join Organization](https://admin.mistral.ai/join) [1].\n  - **Note**: Users still create and manage their own credentials (email and password) [1].\n\n### 2. **Sign-In Without Separate Password Credentials (SSO)**\n- **Supported Plans**: Enterprise only [7].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** is mandatory [5][7].\n  - SAML SSO must be configured with an **identity provider (IdP)** like Okta or Azure AD [7].\n  - Users sign in using their **corporate credentials** without needing a Mistral-specific password [7].\n\n### **Key Differences**\n- **Email Domain Authentication** (Team+) enables **automatic joining** but does not replace password-based authentication [1].\n- **SAML SSO** (Enterprise) enables **passwordless sign-in** via corporate credentials but does not automatically join users unless explicitly configured [7].\n\n### **Combined Setup (If Possible)**\n- To achieve **both automatic joining and passwordless sign-in**, you must:\n  1. Enable **Email Domain Authentication** (Team+) to allow automatic joining [1].\n  2. Enable **SAML SSO** (Enterprise) to replace password-based authentication [7].\n- **Note**: The sources do not explicitly state whether SSO can trigger automatic joining, but SSO does provision users on first sign-in [7].\n\n### **Verified Domain Requirement**\n- Both features require **at least one verified domain** [1][5][7].\n- Domain verification involves adding a **DNS TXT record** [5].\n\n### **Steps to Verify a Domain**\n```\n1. Open [Admin Panel > Administration > Access](https://admin.mistral.ai/organization/access).\n2. Click **Add Domain** in the **Domain Ownership** section.\n3. Enter your domain (e.g., `yourcompany.com`) and click **Add domain**.\n4. Click **Verify domain** and copy the DNS TXT record provided.\n5. Add the TXT record to your DNS provider (e.g., `Type: TXT`, `Host: @`, `Value: mistral-domain-verification=xxxxxx`).\n6. Wait for DNS propagation (10 minutes to 24 hours) [5].\n```",
