  "answer_markdown": "To create a Workspace via the Admin API, the following is required in the request body according to the schema `AdminWorkspaceIn` [4,8]:\n\n- **`name` (string, required)** — The name of the Workspace.\n- **`admin_user_id` (string (uuid), required)** — The User ID of the user to grant the Workspace Admin role to.\n\nOptional fields include:\n- **`description` (string)** — A description of the Workspace.\n- **`icon` (string)** — An icon for the Workspace.\n- **`add_all_org_members` (boolean)** — Whether to add all Organization members to the Workspace.\n\nThe API request must include the following headers:\n- **`Content-Type: application/json`**\n- **`x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY`** — The API key used for this request must be an **Admin API key** [1,8].\n\nThe Admin API key must be created specifically for the Admin API and must have the necessary permissions to manage Workspaces. This key is typically generated via the **Admin API Keys API** [1], where the `workspace_uuid` and `user_id` fields are required for key creation, but the key itself is not tied to a specific Workspace—it is scoped to the **Organization Admin** role [7].\n\nHere is an example of the request to create a Workspace:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.mistral.ai/v1/admin/workspaces \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"name\": \"MySpace\",\n    \"description\": \"Small Workspace\",\n    \"icon\": \"\",\n    \"add_all_org_members\": false,\n    \"admin_user_id\": \"<USER_UUID>\"\n  }'\n```\n\nThe Admin API key must be provided in the `x-api-key` header, and it must be generated with the appropriate permissions for Admin operations [1].",
